  "save": {
    "$note": "The device keeps the journal (which evidence it has seen and shown), the horde clock and its history, the play scores and the paint (key fieldworks-save). It keeps no map: the castle is derived from the evidence each time. A save carries this version and a hash of the rules it was made under; another rules hash loads under the current rules and says so once; a version-1 save (the old fortress map) keeps its journal and says so once; an unreadable save is discarded and the castle still stands on its evidence (pillar 2).",
    "version": 2,
    "autosave_seconds": 5
  },
  "clock": {
    "$note": "The horde clock runs on real days (D25, re-cut by D34): a warning warning_hours ahead and an arrival at horde.arrive_hour in the device's own zone. The prototype steps the day from its dev bar so a horde can be met in a five-minute session. The prototype's clock is day-granular: horde.arrive_hour is the app's, and nothing here reads it yet.",
    "modes": [
      "demo",
      "real"
    ],
    "default": "demo"
  },
  "states": {
    "$note": "Honest states, each reachable from the dev bar: an unread backlog leaves the horde clock unlit (it gathers nothing, never a zero); a dark lane draws from its last read and says how old it is; a quiet week dims the beacon.",
